# Markdown twins: UTF-8, and each one names its HTML page as canonical (Google accepts rel=canonical in an HTTP header for
# non-HTML files), so the twin never competes with the page it mirrors. Three shapes cover every twin:
# /es.md, /es/business.md and /es/s/legal--contract-review.md. One rule each, however many pages there are.
/*.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
/:lang.md
  Link: <https://skills.sgomez.dev/:lang>; rel="canonical"
/:lang/:page.md
  Link: <https://skills.sgomez.dev/:lang/:page>; rel="canonical"
/:lang/s/:slug.md
  Link: <https://skills.sgomez.dev/:lang/s/:slug>; rel="canonical"
